   "id": "b47fe8ae-d438-4875-b670-9331fe91df63",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Financial Markets & Portfolio Risk Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "## Project Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "This project uses Python to evaluate the historical performance and risk characteristics of five major financial assets from 2020–2025.\n",
    "\n",
    "The analysis examines:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Historical prices and daily returns\n",
    "- Annualized return and volatility\n",
    "- Cross-asset correlations\n",
    "- Portfolio diversification\n",
    "- Maximum drawdowns\n",
    "- Risk-adjusted performance using the Sharpe ratio\n",
    "- Growth of a hypothetical $10,000 investment\n",
    "\n",
    "### Assets Analyzed\n",
    "\n",
    "- **SPY** — U.S. large-cap equities\n",
    "- **QQQ** — technology and growth-oriented equities\n",
    "- **TLT** — long-term U.S. Treasury bonds\n",
    "- **GLD** — gold\n",
    "- **BTC-USD** — Bitcoin\n",
    "\n",
    "### Tools\n",
    "\n",
    "Python • Pandas • NumPy • Matplotlib • yfinance"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "7f02770a-9107-4d0e-bd9b-7eb00600566b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Libraries loaded successfully.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import yfinance as yf\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Libraries loaded successfully.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1d23a192-2895-46d1-b539-c3a5e9e320c2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Data Collection\n",
    "\n",
    "Historical market data was retrieved using `yfinance` for five assets representing equities, bonds, gold, and cryptocurrency.\n",
    "\n",
    "The analysis covers **January 2020 through December 2025**. Adjusted market prices are used to account for relevant distributions and corporate actions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
