   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Correlation & Diversification\n",
    "\n",
    "Correlation measures the degree to which asset returns move together.\n",
    "\n",
    "Assets with lower or negative correlations can provide diversification benefits because their prices may respond differently to the same market conditions. A correlation close to **+1** indicates strong positive co-movement, while a value close to **0** indicates little linear relationship."
   ]
  },
