   "source": [
    "### Key Findings\n",
    "\n",
    "- **SPY and QQQ** had a correlation of **0.94**, indicating very strong co-movement and therefore limited diversification between the two equity ETFs.\n",
    "- **Gold** showed relatively weak correlations with SPY (**0.13**), QQQ (**0.14**), and Bitcoin (**0.13**).\n",
    "- **TLT** had slight negative correlations with SPY (**-0.12**), QQQ (**-0.07**), and Bitcoin (**-0.03**).\n",
    "- Bitcoin had moderate positive correlations with SPY (**0.38**) and QQQ (**0.39**), but substantially weaker relationships with Gold and TLT.\n",
    "\n",
    "These relationships demonstrate why combining assets from different asset classes can alter overall portfolio risk."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fe43b652-2cd5-4af3-8dd5-85147d64617d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Equal-Weight Portfolio Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "To evaluate the effect of diversification, an equal-weight portfolio was constructed with **20% allocated to each of the five assets**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The portfolio combines equities, bonds, gold, and cryptocurrency rather than concentrating exposure in a single asset class."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "69537266-e352-40a8-a173-43d882037075",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Date\n",
       "2020-01-03    0.012678\n",
       "2020-01-06    0.014568\n",
       "2020-01-07    0.009368\n",
       "2020-01-08   -0.002307\n",
       "2020-01-09   -0.002348\n",
       "dtype: float64"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 13,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "weights = np.array([0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20, 0.20])\n",
    "\n",
    "portfolio_returns = returns.dot(weights)\n",
    "\n",
    "portfolio_returns.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "ec4c24e6-f0a5-41b5-afb0-150d50be42ff",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Annualized Portfolio Return: 23.32%\n",
      "Annualized Portfolio Volatility: 18.89%\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "portfolio_annual_return = (\n",
    "    (1 + portfolio_returns).prod()\n",
    "    ** (trading_days / len(portfolio_returns))\n",
    ") - 1\n",
    "\n",
    "portfolio_annual_volatility = (\n",
    "    portfolio_returns.std() * np.sqrt(trading_days)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Annualized Portfolio Return: {portfolio_annual_return * 100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Annualized Portfolio Volatility: {portfolio_annual_volatility * 100:.2f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6d3c1f93-70e8-494c-8e83-b0792dc2e614",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Portfolio Performance\n",
    "\n",
    "The equal-weight portfolio generated an annualized historical return of **23.32%** with annualized volatility of **18.89%**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The result illustrates the effect of combining assets with different return and correlation characteristics. Although Bitcoin produced a substantially higher standalone return, the diversified portfolio achieved considerably lower volatility."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d01a1461-9050-468f-87e4-cc73e5ed090e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Downside Risk & Drawdown Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Volatility does not fully describe the severity of investment losses. Drawdown measures the decline in value from a previous peak and provides a more intuitive view of downside risk.\n",
    "\n",
    "Maximum drawdown represents the largest peak-to-trough decline experienced during the analysis period."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "cf92d801-aca2-4b3a-bd20-2e4ce0af03ad",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Maximum Portfolio Drawdown: -37.74%\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "cumulative_portfolio = (1 + portfolio_returns).cumprod()\n",
    "\n",
    "running_peak = cumulative_portfolio.cummax()\n",
    "\n",
    "portfolio_drawdown = (\n",
    "    cumulative_portfolio / running_peak\n",
    ") - 1\n",
    "\n",
    "max_drawdown = portfolio_drawdown.min()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Maximum Portfolio Drawdown: {max_drawdown * 100:.2f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 28,
   "id": "efa7e576-7150-46a7-9822-793cfffcf00f",
