   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Risk-Adjusted Performance\n",
    "\n",
    "The Sharpe ratio is used to compare return relative to the volatility experienced in generating that return.\n",
    "\n",
    "For simplicity and transparency, this analysis assumes a **0% risk-free rate**. Under this assumption, a higher Sharpe ratio indicates greater historical return per unit of volatility."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "f7079359-a8e0-4d04-8267-97a8292af340",
   "metadata": {},
